;; Demo capture for mcp-tkx, driven by screen-grab.
;;
;;   bb demo:record    a GIF per item
;;   bb demo:shot      a still per item
;;
;; The Babashka smoke test is the one thing worth animating here. A still
;; shows six ok lines; a GIF shows a real MCP round trip completing on a
;; runtime that could not load this library at all a day earlier.
;;
;; Terminal is spawned via osascript because screen-grab captures a macOS
;; window, and a bb task on its own has none. `:target {:app "iTerm2"}`
;; rather than the spawned pid, since osascript exits immediately and the
;; window belongs to Terminal.
;;
;; The two scripts/demo-*.sh wrappers exist for one reason: `do script`
;; opens a NEW shell in the user's HOME, so this manifest's :cwd never
;; reaches the recorded command. A bare `bb bb:smoke` there fails with
;; "File does not exist: bb:smoke", because babashka falls back to
;; treating a task name as a script path when no bb.edn is in scope. The
;; wrappers self-locate, so a clone anywhere works and no absolute path
;; has to survive EDN, then sh, then AppleScript quoting.
;;
;; RUN THIS FROM A DIFFERENT TERMINAL APP THAN THE ONE BEING CAPTURED.
;; With :target {:app "iTerm2"}, start it from iTerm2, and vice versa.
;;
;; cgevent resolves :app with `pgrep -x`, and BSD pgrep excludes the
;; calling process AND ITS ANCESTORS unless given -a. Your terminal
;; emulator is an ancestor of anything you type into it, so pgrep cannot
;; see it, and the capture dies with "window never appeared" while the
;; window is plainly on screen. Verified 2026-09-02: `pgrep -x Terminal`
;; found nothing while Terminal ran as pid 3243, and `pgrep -a -x
;; Terminal` returned 3243. Every pid ps could see and pgrep could not
;; was exactly the caller's ancestor chain.
;;
;; The real fix is one flag in cgevent's app->pid
;; (src/net/b12n/cgevent/cli.clj): `pgrep -x` should be `pgrep -a -x`.
;; Until that lands, use a different terminal app.
{:driver   :spawn
 :out-dir  "docs/demos"
 :title    "mcp-tkx demos"
 :preamble "Recorded with screen-grab (https://github.com/burinc/b12n-screen-grab). Regenerate with `bb demo:record`."
 ;; Relative on purpose. bb demo:record runs from the repo root, and the
 ;; demo-*.sh wrappers self-locate, so no absolute path belongs in here.
 :cwd      "."
 ;; 15s covers the wrapper: 3s lead-in, the run (sub-second warm, a few
 ;; seconds cold), then its 9s hold on the result. Do not widen it much
 ;; further or the tail is a static prompt.
 :defaults {:duration 15 :fps 12 :width 900 :warmup 20}
 :examples
 [{:id     "bb-smoke"
   :group  "babashka"
   :desc   "`bb bb:smoke` driving a real tools/list and tools/call through a server session on Babashka. Six checks, and the round trip completing is the point: loading proves nothing here, because both problems it guards against sit behind a require that succeeds."
   :src    "dev/bb_smoke.clj"
   :target {:app "iTerm2"}
   :run    "sh scripts/demo-open-terminal.sh"}]
 :groups [{:key "babashka" :title "Babashka"}]}
